# /etc/network/interfaces — multiprox node (build-time placeholder)
#
# Deliberately minimal. setup-bridge.sh REPLACES this file at container start,
# once it can see which interface Docker attached to the guest network and which
# address it holds. Neither is knowable at build time.
#
# Until then this must be inert. ifupdown may run before setup-bridge on some
# boots, and anything describing eth0 here is a hazard: eth0 is the veth Docker
# configured, and it carries Corosync, the Ceph public network, pmxcfs and the
# web UI. A DHCP stanza would hang (Docker networks have no DHCP server) and a
# `bridge-ports eth0` stanza would flush the address the cluster depends on.
#
# See scripts/setup-bridge.sh for the vmbr0 layout that replaces this.

auto lo
iface lo inet loopback
